    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: da334d1297ca1895c46b14e1f00bb4893a2d173e -->\n**Maintainer-requested shallow verification (Windows): clean.** `cargo test -p xtask`: 13 passed. `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -D warnings`: clean. Dry-run plans against origin/main's `gate.ps1`: batch 18/18 and release 26/26 lines, identical. Quick on a sample diff: identical (it falls back to batch on both, because this branch touches `Cargo.toml`). Real run: `cargo xtask gate test tools_bin_lists_a_sane_catalog --crate tools --exact` ok, exit 0. Wrappers: `gate.ps1 -Tier batch -DryRun` and `DRY_RUN=1 gate.sh batch` both plan 9 steps. Not exercised: macOS and Linux, and real quick/batch/release runs. The maintainer approved the `regex` dependency and the scripts change by asking for this check and merge.",
